4114                 /       ALL WORDS FROM 7750-7777 ARE AVAILABLE AT BOOTSTRAP TIME FOR
4115                 /       HANDLER INITIALIZATION AS WELL AS 7600-7607 AND 7632-7640.
4116                 /       IT IS THE RESPONSIBILIY OF THE HANDLER TO GET 7602 (SBTFUN) PROPERLY
4117                 /       FORMATTED AS THE BOOTSTRAP UNIT WORD AND 7632-7637 (SLOAD-SYSTART)
4118                 /       PROPERLY FORMATTED AS THE SYSTEM LOADER TO THE CORRECT UNIT TO SAVE CORE IN
4119                 /       %:[BOOTSTRAP UNIT] AND $:[BOOTSTRAP UNIT].
4120   
4121                 /       OPERATION OF THE SYSTEM WILL STORE INTO 7604-7607 (SWAL-SOUTFLS),
4122                 /       7632-7637 (SLOAD-SYSTART), AND 7756-7777 (SPARM-SFILES+20).
4123   
4124                 /       THE SYSTEM DATE AND CORE SIZE WORDS (7610-7611) WILL BE UPDATED ALSO AND ARE
4125                 /       EXPECTED TO BE AVAILABLE AS IS.
